# Chip / pill label soft hyphens

When a label in a **fixed-width pill, chip, or 2-column tag grid** overflows because one Spanish word is too long (e.g. “Estacionamiento”), do **not** shrink font size, force `whitespace-nowrap`, or rely on `break-all` (ugly mid-syllable cuts without a dash).

## Preferred fix: soft hyphen (U+00AD)

Insert a **soft hyphen** at a sensible syllable break. It stays invisible when the word fits on one line; when the line wraps at that point, the browser shows a visible `-`.

```ts
import { SOFT_HYPHEN } from "@/lib/listingTags";

// Renders as "Estacionamiento" when it fits, or "Estacionami-" / "ento …" when it wraps.
`Estacionami${SOFT_HYPHEN}ento privado`
```

Canonical constant: `SOFT_HYPHEN` in `src/lib/listingTags.ts`.

## Pair with layout so wrapping can happen

On grid/flex chip buttons that hold wrapping text:

- Add `min-w-0` so CSS grid/flex items may shrink below the unbreakable min-content width.
- Prefer `hyphens-manual` so only soft hyphens you inserted act as break points (not automatic language hyphenation).

Example classes: `min-w-0 … hyphens-manual text-left text-xs`.

## When to apply

- Publish wizard / room editor tag pills (`Propiedades de la recámara`, amenity grids).
- Any similar rounded-full choice chip where mobile half-width columns clip long words.
- Add new soft-hyphen points in the **shared label maps** (`LISTING_TAG_LABEL_OVERRIDES`, `TAG_LABELS`, etc.) when you discover another overflowing word — do not hardcode a line break only in one screen.

## Avoid

- Hard `<br />` or forced `\n` (always two lines even on wide layouts).
- `break-all` / `break-words` alone for Spanish compound words (no hyphen, poor readability).
- Inventing a shorter marketing synonym just to dodge overflow when soft hyphening keeps the correct term.
